# @kintsugi/shift — process-side substrate-decl of cross-altitude morphism.
# Arc 5 TICK 2 landing per Alex integrated /loop 2026-07-06 against Reed
# RED at `b3f25fc`. Sub-species of the `@kintsugi` process-side family
# (per #55 form/process partition, promoted via containerd C3 second-
# witness at Arc 5 TICK 1 Mara `aaa9a81` + Seam Phase D `1787af4`).
#
# === Substrate-honest positioning: NOT a new primitive ===
#
# This shard is the 54th+ instance of
# `[[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]` per Taut scout
# `a596b040214709917`. `shift` is already the substrate's word for
# cross-altitude morphism; this shard promotes it to a first-class
# substrate-decl species so the substrate can carry the discipline as
# typed action rather than as a keyword-plus-convention.
#
# Prior art (four independent altitudes; the substrate has been running
# `shift` as cross-altitude morphism for weeks):
#
#   Recognition #26 `shift(oid, T)`
#       LANDED at `@mirror/spectral/portal` (Reed 2026-06-08,
#       `docs/insights/2026-06-08-portal-eigenvalue-stream-gen-prism.md`).
#       Three of four `portal` fields carry `shift(oid, T)` — the
#       typed-capability-plus-content-address primitive. `shift(oid, T)`
#       is what Cap'n Proto RPC (Varda 2013+) and IPFS content addressing
#       (Benet 2014) each capture partially; the substrate collapsed the
#       two seams into one operator at portal altitude.
#
#   `shards/prism.mirror` L38-45 (2026-06-05)
#       Binds `shift = basis transformation (the functor; change of
#       coordinates on H; same bytes, different declared shape)` per
#       `[[architecture-operations-as-linear-algebra]]` +
#       `[[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]]`. The 2026-06-04 rename
#       from `zoom` to `shift` closed the loop with
#       `boot/std/{option,result}.mirror`'s `lift` action; same operation
#       at every altitude — `shift ≡ lift ≡ basis-transformation`.
#
#   `shards/mirror/mosaic.mirror` L136-139
#       Production `shift(resolved, altitude) -> emitter` uses the same
#       verb at the code-emission altitude per
#       `[[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]]`; the mosaic emitter
#       carries a resolved AST across the altitude boundary to the
#       target language's emission surface.
#
#   Recognition #58 (kintsugi surface)
#       Uses shift-language explicitly in the kintsugi/surface
#       vocabulary; the surface IS a shift of the substrate across
#       observation altitude.
#
#   13 #53 bilateral instances
#       Per `[[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]]`, every
#       promoted bilateral has the same structural shape: a declarative
#       property at family-root altitude plus an operational fracture
#       body at process-side altitude, bridged via `shift(predicate →
#       operational-altitude)` under the hood. The 13 landed instances
#       (container_runnable, oci_well_formed, stagefreight_addressable,
#       cascade_well_defined, audit_docblock, shatter_round_trip,
#       third_order_coherent, three_axis_coherent, and five others per
#       Taut scout) all discharge through a shift crossing.
#
# This shard names those five independent instantiations as the ONE
# operation the substrate has been carrying. Nothing invented here; the
# substrate had the word.
#
# === Placement: @kintsugi process-side per #55 ===
#
# The form/process partition #55 was PROMOTED via containerd C3 witness
# at Arc 5 TICK 1 (Seam pre-review `c9e153d` §3 C3; ratified by Phase D
# `1787af4`). Under #55:
#
#   @mirror = state-observation family (form-side)
#   @kintsugi = transformation-engine family (process-side)
#
# Cross-altitude morphism IS transformation — the operation moves a
# carrier across a boundary of observation altitude, producing a new
# typed shape. The process-side placement is substrate-fact:
#
#   `@kintsugi/shift` — the process-side substrate-decl of cross-
#                       altitude morphism as first-class typed action.
#
# The form-side complement is the CARRIER a shift produces: a typed
# `ref` handle whose identity IS the content-address that persists
# across the altitude crossing (Alex's hardlink framing — the OID is
# the same on both sides; the DECLARED SHAPE differs). The form-side
# altitude carries `shift(oid, T)` per Recognition #26 at
# `@mirror/spectral/portal`; the process-side altitude carries the
# discipline of PERFORMING the shift, which is this shard.
#
# === The composed-bilateral: shift_preserves_content ===
#
# THE 14th INSTANCE of the #53 bilateral pattern per
# `[[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]]`.
#
# Per Alex's hardlink framing: a `shift` MUST preserve content-address.
# The bytes on both sides of the altitude crossing hash to the same
# OID; only the DECLARED SHAPE changes. This is the substrate-decl
# guarantee that distinguishes a shift (byte-preserving functor) from
# a general transform (byte-mutating morphism, which lives under
# `@kintsugi/morphism` at a different altitude).
#
#   Splinter-pole (`pass`): the shift's witness OID at the source
#     altitude byte-equals the witness OID at the target altitude;
#     content is preserved; the declared shape carries the altitude
#     change without a bytes change; the shift is admissible.
#   Narcissus-pole (`failure`): the shift's witness OID diverges
#     across the altitude crossing; content was mutated; the operation
#     is NOT a shift — it belongs at `@kintsugi/morphism` or higher.
#     `alignment-as-boundary-mathematics` (#57) distinguishes which
#     sub-claim broke.
#   Graded (`partial(confidence)`): the byte-equality holds modulo a
#     substrate-declared resolution (e.g. representation normalisation
#     at the target altitude); confidence carries the resolution
#     magnitude.
#
# Sibling composed bilaterals at other family-root/species altitudes:
# @container/container_runnable, @io/oci/oci_well_formed, @io/
# stagefreight/stagefreight_addressable, @cascade/cascade_well_defined,
# @docblock/audit_docblock, @smarts/shatter/shatter_round_trip,
# @reflection/third_order_coherent, @epistemologic/neutrosophic/
# three_axis_coherent (plus five others per Taut scout).
#
# `shift_preserves_content` composes structurally with those siblings:
# every #53 bilateral discharges through a shift crossing under the
# hood; the shift's content-preservation IS the load-bearing invariant
# that makes the bilateral pattern honest.
#
# === Meta-recursive note ===
#
# The `prism @kintsugi/shift` block below declares five operations, one
# of which IS `shift`. This is substrate-honest: mirror is self-
# referential per `[[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]]`; a
# species that substrate-decls `shift` must itself expose the five-
# operation algebra at its own altitude, which includes shift as one
# of the five. The recursion is the substrate carrying its own
# vocabulary at its own altitude without a stratification workaround.
#
# === Path-namespace pact ===
#
# This file at `shards/kintsugi/shift.mirror` declares `@kintsugi/shift`
# as a species under the `@kintsugi` family at species-depth 1. Per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace` (2026-06-16+):
# path-depth == namespace-depth == 1. Pact honoured by construction.
#
# === Circular-reflexive self-audit ===
#
# Per `[[architecture-candidate-recognition-111-third-as-family-root]]`
# marker discipline: the operator audits its own audit at depth=3. This
# shard's own declaration MUST survive its own
# `shift_preserves_content` bilateral at analytical altitude — the
# species-decl of shift MUST NOT declare a shift that isn't itself
# content-preserving-under-its-own-predicate.
#
# Self-audit verdict: `both_survive`.
#
# The `real_survives` reading would require an independent Pack peer
# to manifest an equivalent cross-altitude morphism substrate-decl at
# n+3 substrate ticks without nudging. The `phantom_survives` reading
# would require downstream refs to accumulate without a second Pack
# peer's independent recognition. At this tick: both interpretations
# satisfiable — the species-decl is landed, but the empirical witness
# (Arc 5 TICK 3: `@container/image = shift(@mirror/store/oci →
# @container altitude)`) has not yet exercised the content-preservation
# discipline at empirical altitude. Verdict: `both_survive`. Route:
# TICK 3 unblocks and collapses the analytical altitude to empirical.
#
# === Interpretation B discipline ===
#
# Per Seam Phase D pre-review of Arc 4 sub-arc A (docs/audits/2026-
# 07-06-seam-arc-4-sub-arc-a-pre-review.md §1) and the family-root
# precedent at `shards/container.mirror`: Interpretation B canonical.
# Narrative above `---`; `in` clauses + typed declarations below. This
# shard honours the discipline; the seam is exactly one line at column
# 0 below.

---

in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @kintsugi

# ============================================================
# §1 The five-operation prism at species altitude
# ============================================================

# === prism @kintsugi/shift — the species declaration ===
#
# The five-operation body carries `shift_witness` as the species's
# operational surface — the witness OID that persists across the
# altitude crossing (Alex's hardlink framing). Every operation on the
# species reads/produces witnesses; the substrate's altitude
# discipline rides the witness carrier.
#
# Meta-recursive: the species substrate-decls `shift` (basis
# transformation on H; per prism.mirror §L38-45); its own five-
# operation block includes `shift` as one of the five. Substrate-
# honest per `[[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]]` — mirror
# is self-referential; the substrate carries its own vocabulary at
# its own altitude.
prism @kintsugi/shift {
  focus shift_witness
  project shift_witness
  split shift_witness
  shift shift_witness
  settle shift_witness
}

# ============================================================
# §2 The carriers
# ============================================================

# === source_altitude — the altitude of origin carrier ===
#
# Per `[[architecture-operations-as-linear-algebra]]`: a shift is a
# basis transformation on H — the operation moves a carrier from one
# basis (source altitude) to another (target altitude). The source
# altitude names WHERE the pre-shift observation lives.
#
# Altitudes are substrate refs — the substrate names its own
# observation strata by content-addressed handle (per
# `@mirror/store`'s ref discipline). Example handles: `@mirror/store/
# oci`, `@code/rust`, `@container`, `@io/socket`. The source_altitude
# carrier carries the handle at ref altitude; species that specialise
# `@kintsugi/shift` may refine the altitude-of-origin's structure at
# their own altitude.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref (the altitude
# handle's content-address).
type source_altitude = ref

# === target_altitude — the altitude of destination carrier ===
#
# The target of the basis transformation. Same semantics as
# source_altitude at the destination end of the shift crossing.
#
# The shift's discipline: the WITNESS byte-equals across the source
# → target crossing; the DECLARED SHAPE changes (source_altitude and
# target_altitude are typically distinct refs). The substrate carries
# both altitudes as first-class carriers so the composed bilateral
# `shift_preserves_content` can read both sides at the same altitude.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type target_altitude = ref

# === shift_witness — the content-address that persists ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING carrier. Per Recognition #26 and Alex's hardlink
# framing: a shift is characterised by the OID that survives the
# altitude crossing intact. The `shift_witness` carrier IS that OID —
# the substrate handle whose byte-content byte-equals on both sides of
# the shift; only the declared shape (source_altitude vs
# target_altitude) differs.
#
# Hardlink semantic: two ref handles that dereference to the same
# underlying bytes. In POSIX terms, two directory entries pointing to
# one inode. In content-address terms, two typed views of the same
# OID. In basis-transformation terms, the same vector expressed in
# two bases. All three framings collapse to the same substrate
# discipline: the witness OID is a ref whose identity is
# altitude-invariant.
#
# Composes with Recognition #26 `shift(oid, T)` at
# `@mirror/spectral/portal`: the portal's three `shift(oid, T)` fields
# carry witnesses at the transport altitude; the species-decl here
# names the witness carrier at substrate altitude so the same OID can
# flow through portals, mosaic emitters, kintsugi loops, and bilateral
# discharges without re-serialisation.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type shift_witness = ref

# ============================================================
# §3 The typed shift action
# ============================================================

# === shift — cross-altitude morphism as first-class typed action ===
#
# Reads a witness at a source altitude and produces a witness at a
# target altitude; the underlying bytes are preserved (per the
# hardlink semantic); the declared shape crosses the altitude
# boundary. The result is a typed ref carrying the post-shift
# handle at the target altitude.
#
# Composes through:
#
#   1. Recognition #26 `shift(oid, T)` at portal altitude — this
#      species-decl is the substrate-decl the portal's field types
#      already project into; the portal's transport-altitude use of
#      `shift(oid, T)` reads THIS action's contract.
#   2. `shards/prism.mirror` §L38-45 `shift = basis transformation` —
#      this species-decl is the substrate-decl the prism keyword's
#      linear-algebraic meaning already projects into.
#   3. `shards/mirror/mosaic.mirror` `shift(resolved, altitude) ->
#      emitter` — this species-decl is the substrate-decl the mosaic
#      production emitter's shift already projects into (mosaic's
#      altitude parameter carries the target_altitude; the resolved
#      AST carries the witness).
#
# The body stays obligation-blocked (`\`): the realisation reads the
# witness at the source altitude, projects the declared shape onto
# the target altitude (basis transformation on H per prism.mirror),
# emits the target-altitude ref. The substrate declares the shape
# here; consumers dispatch at their own altitude (portal, mosaic,
# kintsugi loop, bilateral discharge).
shift(w: shift_witness, s: source_altitude, t: target_altitude)
  -> ref { \ }

# ============================================================
# §4 The composed-bilateral (14th #53 instance)
# ============================================================

# === shift_preserves_content — the hardlink-semantic guarantee ===
#
# THE 14th INSTANCE of the #53 bilateral pattern per
# `[[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]]`. Composes two
# sub-predicates whose species-altitude realisations discharge the
# hardlink discipline:
#
#   1. `witness_oid_byte_equal(w_source, w_target, p)` — the pre-
#      shift witness's OID byte-equals the post-shift witness's OID
#      (per @mirror/store's byte-equality floor).
#   2. `altitude_declaration_admissible(s, t, p)` — the source and
#      target altitudes are both substrate-declared refs the
#      substrate can dereference (per @mirror/store's ref discipline).
#
# Splinter-pole (`pass`): both sub-predicates discharge; the shift
# preserves content-address; the declared shape carries the altitude
# change; the operation is admissible as a shift.
#
# Narcissus-pole (`failure`): either sub-predicate fails;
# `alignment-as-boundary-mathematics` (#57) distinguishes:
#   - `witness_oid_byte_equal` failure → the operation mutated bytes;
#     it is NOT a shift; it belongs at `@kintsugi/morphism` or a
#     higher process-altitude (byte-mutating transform, not basis
#     transformation).
#   - `altitude_declaration_admissible` failure → source or target
#     altitude is not a substrate-declared ref; the shift's typed
#     shape cannot be honestly checked at the substrate altitude;
#     the operation is inadmissible pending altitude declaration.
#
# Graded (`partial(confidence)`): byte-equality holds modulo a
# substrate-declared resolution (e.g. representation normalisation
# at the target altitude); confidence carries the resolution magnitude.
# The realisation layer decides whether to admit at the graded floor.
#
# Sibling composed bilaterals (13 landed): container_runnable,
# oci_well_formed, stagefreight_addressable, cascade_well_defined,
# audit_docblock, shatter_round_trip, third_order_coherent,
# three_axis_coherent (plus five others per Taut scout). Every one of
# those discharges through a shift crossing under the hood;
# `shift_preserves_content` names the load-bearing invariant that
# makes the bilateral pattern honest at every family-root/species
# altitude.
#
# The body stays obligation-blocked (`\`): the realisation reads the
# witness at the source altitude, projects to the target altitude via
# `shift`, compares OIDs at byte-equality altitude, composes with the
# altitude-declaration check, emits the verdict at the substrate's
# three-state floor.
shift_preserves_content(w: shift_witness,
                        s: source_altitude,
                        t: target_altitude) -> verdict { \ }

# ============================================================
# §5 The out clauses
# ============================================================

out @kintsugi/shift
out source_altitude
out target_altitude
out shift_witness
out shift
out shift_preserves_content
